#
# JIT inline directives for jinfer's hot Vector API helpers.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES. These small methods return or consume jdk.incubator.vector values. When the JIT does not
# inline one into its hot loop, the vector escapes the method boundary and is boxed - a FloatVector object plus
# its backing float[] per call - instead of being scalar-replaced into a SIMD register. A strong inliner
# (Oracle GraalVM) does it unprompted; a weaker one may not: plain C2 under budget pressure here, and GraalVM's
# AOT inliner, which needs the same calls held open by @AlwaysInline (see jinfer-kernels' native-image.properties
# - that one is a 57x cliff, not a few percent). Forcing the inline makes the loop allocation-free.
#
# THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT INSTRUMENT, never a requirement. jinfer must be fast on a stock JVM with no flags,
# and a kernel that is only fast with these hints is a bug in the kernel. Do not add an entry to paper over one,
# and do not add one you have not measured - two of the three notes below exist because that was done anyway.
#
# LEAVES ONLY, NEVER TILE BODIES. A leaf is a few instructions returning one vector; inlining it removes a
# boundary the vector would otherwise cross. A tile body is already a large compilation unit, and forcing it
# into its caller pushes that unit past what the JIT will expand, so the vectors box wholesale. The qkTile* and
# pvTile* entries were removed on 2026-09-07 after measuring, per 512x512 image on LFM2.5-VL-3B and per
# 565-token prefill on LFM2.5-8B-A1B-Q4_K_M:
#
#                          vision prefill        text prefill
#                       Graal        C2        Graal       C2
#   no flags            1059 ms    1612 ms    1120 t/s   1168 t/s
#   with tile bodies    3023 ms    9220 ms    1192 t/s   1204 t/s
#   leaves only         1054 ms    1592 ms    1207 t/s   1193 t/s
#
# Removing them cost text prefill nothing and took vision prefill off a 2.9x/5.7x cliff.
#
# HOW TO MEASURE THIS FILE. Pass -Djam.native.disabled=true: these are Vector API helpers, and with jam-native
# present its C kernels carry the prefill GEMM and hide the Java path entirely (1235 t/s against 487 on the
# vector backend - the A/B run that way shows nothing either way). Alternate the arms and compare pairs within
# a run rather than columns; both drift down together over a 20-minute session as the box heats, by more than
# the effect under test. And measure VISION as well as text: the two cliffs recorded here are vision-only, and
# a text-prefill A/B cannot see them.
#
# Last measured 2026-09-09 against the list below, LFM2.5-2.6B-Q8_0, jinfer-bench -p 512 -r 5, three runs per
# arm on the vector backend: without this file 493.3 / 488.8 / 488.4 t/s, with it 491.2 / 489.0 / 486.0,
# paired -0.4% / +0.0% / -0.5%. No gain and no loss on that JIT.
#
# CAVEAT ON THE JVM USED. These numbers, and the pvTile ones below, come from a LOCALLY BUILT, PATCHED GraalVM
# CE - 25.4.4.1.1-dev+1.1, graal at 22d016e97a2, carrying the 32-ZMM register work - not from any released CE.
# Its inliner and register allocator differ from a stock build, so treat the figures as "no effect on that
# compiler" rather than as a statement about GraalVM CE releases. A stock CE has not been measured here.
# (A "+~45% on GraalVM CE" figure this header carried until 2026-09-08 predated the current entry list and did
# not reproduce on the patched build; do not restore it from memory.)
#
# EXCLUDED ON PURPOSE, beyond the tile bodies above:
#   - Convert.f16ToF32Vector and f16BitsToF32: see the NOTE below. Added 2026-09-08 by mirroring the
#     @AlwaysInline set without reading that note, and removed again the same day.
#   - FlashAttention.pvTile, the thin dispatcher branching to pvTileF16/pvTileF32. It keeps its @AlwaysInline,
#     which binds only the AOT compiler, and measured neutral there: native images built with and without it
#     (same patched CE, see the caveat above), LFM2.5-VL-3B-Q8_0 + mmproj-F16 on a 519x600 image, three runs
#     each, gave media cold 458.0 vs 446.1 ms, warm 111.0 vs 107.8, pp512 1190.5 vs 1176.1 t/s - 1-3%,
#     overlapping ranges, opposite directions.
#   - FlashAttention.srcFloat, a scalar accessor rather than a vector helper; nothing for the JIT to hold open.
#
# Use with:  -XX:CompileCommandFile=<path>/hotspot_compile_commands
# Format:    one "inline <class-with-slashes>.<method>" per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Stock C2 alternative (no per-method list): -XX:InlineSmallCode=1000000 alone recovers the same
# prefill (741 vs 756 t/s, LFM 8B Q4_K_M pp512; no-flags baseline 516). Root cause: the vector-
# returning helpers hit compile thresholds before their callers (leaf methods run 64x more), their
# standalone nmethods are bloated by boxing, and C2 then refuses to inline them ("already compiled
# into a big method" / "callee uses too much stack") - raising the size heuristics
# (FreqInlineSize/MaxInlineSize) does nothing because this check fires first. Decode needs no
# flags at all: MatMul routes the C2-hostile k-quant dots to JAM.
#
# NOTE: Convert.f16ToF32Vector is deliberately NOT force-inlined: loadF16 (below) is, and the tiny
# converter goes into it naturally. Force-inlining the converter AT EVERY CALL SITE blows the
# compilation units it lands in - measured twice, and it is the same cliff as the tile bodies above.
# 2026-08: on top of the then-forced qkTile/pvTile bodies it made qwen35's hybrid attention layers
# 2.0x SLOWER on Oracle GraalVM 25.1 (863 vs 1776 t/s, Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q8_0); the regression needed
# BOTH that line and the tile-body lines, which is why those are gone now. 2026-09-07: added on its
# own to the entries below, one 512x512 image on LFM2.5-VL-3B went from 3023 ms to 19825 ms and from
# 83 GB to 712 GB allocated. Leave it out.
